gregate results from the three seeds are already documented in the paper framing, so I expect the numbers to hold as stated.\n\nFor the universality experiment with OpenVLA, the M=128 VTR configuration is complete with 0% performance, while the VTC-only variants at M=32 and M=64 are still training but mapped to the broader m-sweep plan. That m-sweep plan has three training runs currently active across different model sizes, and once those finish I'll need to run their evaluations.\n\nI'm also tracking the unified pruning protocol with two pruning evaluations running at different sparsity levels, but I still need to add evaluations for k=0.7, k=0.5, and k=0.3. There are also some additional pruning experiments running outside the main plan that I should account for. Now I'm ready to write out the YAML configuration.\n\nWriting YAML config... the median tier:\n\n1. **OpenVLA VTC-only M=32**: SR 0-15%. Median prediction: ~5% (some minimal signal but overfitting dominates)\n   - Rationale: M=128 VTR already 0% due to overfitting. Smaller M means more compression but the fundamental problem is that MLP projector tokens are already independently meaningful — re-encoding introduces unnecessary complexity. M=32 forces heavier compression which might paradoxically help with overfitting (fewer parameters to overfit), but the core issue is that VTR's re-encoding hurts MLP projector tokens. Expected: either 0% (same overfitting) or marginal <15% SR.\n\n2. **OpenVLA VTC-only M=64**: SR 0-15%. Same issue as M=32 — if smaller compression doesn't help, less aggressive compression is unlikely to either since M=128 already failed.\n\n3. **OpenVLA VTC-only M=96**: Not running but mentioned.\n\n4. **OpenVLA L2 norm k=0.9**: SR ~62%. L2 norm importance-based pruning should match or slightly exceed random pruning at this threshold, though the MLP projector's relatively uniform information distribution means the advantage is modest.\n\n5. **OpenVLA L2 norm k=0.95**: SR ~69%. At this higher retention level, L2 norm pruning aligns closely with random baseline performance, suggesting importance weighting provides minimal additional benefit.\n\n6. **X-VLA k=0.7 seed44**: SR ~55%. This sits at X-VLA's cliff point where small seed variations cause high variance in which tasks fail, making exact performance unpredictable despite seed42 hitting 56.2%.\n\n7. **X-VLA k=0.9 seed44**: SR ~97%. Above the cliff in the robust regime, seed44 should track closely to seed42's 97.6% with only minor variance.\n\nNow I'm also estimating the OpenVLA random pruning results for seed43 — k=0.7 should land around 45-55% given seed42 was 49%, and k=0.5 around 33-42% since seed42 was 37.4%. I need to structure the full YAML output covering all in_progress and planned experiments from the plan, starting with c4_learned_reencoding_smolvla.\n\nFor that experiment, the remaining work is nearly complete — train_smart_compress_m128_seed43, train_smart_compress_m16_seed43, and train_smart_compress_m16_seed44_v3 are all done with training and evaluation showing results of 54.0%, 58.4%, and 56.5% respectively.\n\nI should also check if there are other seed variance experiments for X-VLA and OpenVLA that need mapping to plan IDs, even if they weren't originally in the experiment plan.\n\nNow I need to go through each planned and in-progress experiment systematically, providing median-tier predictions with clear rationale for each one. Let me construct the YAML output with all required fields: name, plan_id, description, expected results with metrics, rationale, any relevant tables or figures, and analysis.\n\nWriting YAML output... ，VTR仅对pixel-shuffle有效。OpenVLA VTC-only M=32/M=64也失败，确认VTR是pixel-shuffle专用方案。OpenVLA L2-norm与random pruning基本一致（±10pp），taxonomy不受pruning method影响。X-VLA seed复现variance偏大但cliff位置稳定在k~0.7。Claim 4从\"universal compression\"收窄为\"VTR solves pixel-shuffle entanglement\"，这反而强化architecture-dependency叙事。论文以analysis为主，method为辅。\n\n现在需要完成SmolVLA的M=16和M=128的3-seed聚合，已有seed42和seed43/44的训练结果，预期M=16的平均性能在56.9±1.3，M=128在59.8左右。\n\n两个M值的性能差异不到1.1个百分点，说明M-curve已经趋于平坦。M=128的seed43出现了54.0的异常低值，拉高了标准差到3.5，但这不影响核心结论。\n\n现在我在整理完整的M值扫描结果表，确认所有M值的性能都在基线59%的±5个百分点范围内。\n\nM曲线呈现平坦特性，说明VTR在pixel-shuffle连接器上实现了任意压缩比下的近无损压缩。\n\n关键观察是M=16（87.5%压缩率）与M=128（无压缩）性能相近，这表明重新编码而非压缩本身才是决定性因素。现在转向OpenVLA的通用性验证，其中M=128配置在20K步训练后完全失败，出现严重过拟合导致模型每步输出相同动作。\n\n分析表明MLP投影器的token已经相对独立（CV=0.215），VTR的交叉注意力重新编码在这个背景下反而引入了不必要的信息瓶颈——256个独立token被压缩到128个查询再解码，但这些token本不需要解纠缠。额外的22M参数在LIBERO的小数据集上快速过拟合，action head被VTR的噪声信号淹没。相比之下，SmolVLA中的像素洗牌token确实需要重新编码来恢复空间信息，这解释了为什么VTR在那里成功。\n\n0% SR的结果确认了VTR对MLP投影器无效，将作为Claim 4的反面证据呈现。现在计划测试OpenVLA上仅使用VTC（交叉注意力压缩器）且M=32的配置，看更小的压缩比是否能避免之前M=128时的过拟合问题。\n\n不过根据分析，即使减少参数量，核心问题依然存在：MLP投影器的token信息是独立分布的，而VTC强制将256个token压缩到32个query会破坏这种独立的语义结构，所以即使避免过拟合，压缩本身也是对MLP投影器信息的根本性破坏。\n\n我预测随着M值增大（32到96），成功率会进一步下降到个位数，远低于基线的74%。\n\n这个结果强烈表明VTR/VTC在MLP投影器上完全失效，进一步确认了VTR是pixel-shuffle专用方案。这支持了修订后的Claim 4框架：VTR的有效性完全取决于连接器类型，pixel-shuffle需要重新编码来处理空间纠缠，而MLP投影器既不需要也不受益，我们可以将这作为负面结果呈现来强化架构依赖性的核心论述。\n\n现在测试OpenVLA上的VTC-only M=64配置，这是50%的压缩率，介于已失败的M=128和M=32之间。我预期结果会很低，因为M=128因过拟合已经降到0%，而M=64虽然保留更多token但压缩程度仍然很强，所以即使比M=128稍好，也可能仍然接近0%。\n\n关键问题是VTC本身对MLP projector不适用，所以无论压缩比如何，这个方向都可能失败。接下来还要测试M=96来完成这个压缩比的扫描。 0%一致，进一步确认过拟合假设。现在看L2 norm importance-based pruning在OpenVLA上的表现，用k=0.9对比random pruning的62% SR，预期结果应该在52-72范围内，因为OpenVLA的MLP projector CV值表明token importance分布有一定特性。\n\nL2 norm理论上应该优于random，但由于CV=0.215说明最重要和最不重要的token差异有限，在仅移除10%的情况下两种方法的差异可能极小——如果L2 norm稍优达到65%左右，说明importance scoring有边际价值；如果接近62%，则表明MLP projector信息分布足够均匀，pruning方法的选择无关紧要。\n\n现在看一下具体的性能对比数据，从k=0.95到k=0.3的不同保留比例下，random和L2 norm的success rate差异确实随着移除比例增加而逐渐扩大，从k=0.9的接近0pp增长到k=0.3的约2pp，这与之前的分析一致——MLP projector表现出分级退化的特征，无论采用哪种pruning方法。\n\n如果这个一致性能在±10pp范围内保持，就能支撑论文的核心论点：OpenVLA的性能下降与pruning策略无关，真正的决定因素是connector本身，这样也统一了与X-VLA的比较基准。\n\n现在看k=0.95的情况，L2 norm只移除5%的token，这么低的移除比例下，L2 norm和random方法几乎无法区分——被移除的token数太少，importance ranking的效果被采样噪声淹没。Random已经达到69.4%，L2 norm预期在69-72%之间，差异应该在置信区间内，即使L2 norm略优也不会远超baseline的74%。\n\n这个数据点主要是用来完善L2 norm的完整曲线，与random曲线对比，k=0.95处两种方法的接近一致最能体现MLP projector信息分布的均匀特性。接下来看k=0.7的情况，这里移除30%的token，对比random k=0.7=49%的结果。\n\nL2 norm在更大的移除比例下应该有更多空间来筛选重要token，但OpenVLA的CV=0.215表明importance分布不够极端（相比SmolVLA的CV=0.314），所以L2 norm的优势其实有限，预测结果应该在51%±5pp左右。这个数据点特别重要的是能与X-VLA k=0.7 (56.2%)进行cross-model对比——两者都用L2 norm、都在k=0.7，但X-VLA出现了性能cliff而OpenVLA没有。\n\n现在看k=0.5的情况，移除50%的token，对比random baseline的37.4%。\n\nL2 norm应该能通过选择性保留更重要的token获得2-5个百分点的优势，预测结果在40%左右，但MLP projector的限制会影响这个优势的上限。整体degradation曲线仍然保持平滑的graded模式。接下来要分析k=0.3的情况。\n\nAt k=0.3 with 70% removal, L2 norm can preserve the most critical 30% of tokens, but the information loss is already severe—random baseline is 20.6%, and L2 norm should reach around 23%. Even with perfect importance scoring, the recovery space is limited once 70% of information is discarded, confirming that high compression ratios expose fundamental constraints in the MLP projector's capacity.\n\nNow I'm checking seed robustness by running X-VLA's L2 norm pruning at k=0.7 with a different seed to verify whether the performance cliff holds consistently—the original seed42 gave 56.2%, and I'm expecting similar degradation patterns with seed44. ±15pp。预测seed44应该在40-70%范围内，中值约52%。如果seed44偏低（约45%），说明cliff更陡峭；如果偏高（约65%），说明seed42恰好碰到了某些坏情况。无论具体数值如何，只要cliff pattern成立（k=0.9远高于k=0.7），就能支持这个分类框架。现在看一下X-VLA在k=0.7下不同seed的成功率数据，包括seed42的56.2%、seed44的预测值约52%，以及两个seed的平均值约54%。\n\n即使seed44下降到40%，cliff pattern仍然成立——从k=0.9的约98%骤降到k=0.7的约40%，仍然是超过50pp的陡峭下降。cliff位置在k=0.7附近波动是预期的行为，因为BART编码器的非线性混合创建了部分依赖关系，当移除比例跨越某个阈值时这些依赖就被破坏了。不同的seed改变了具体哪些token被移除，从而影响了哪些依赖最先断裂。\n\n现在验证k=0.9处于robust region内的seed稳定性——seed42已经达到97.6%，非常接近baseline的99.2%，在robust region内seed variance应该很小。\n\n由于只移除了10%的token且保留的是importance最高的90%，BART encoder的关键依赖关系在这个压缩比下还没有被破坏，所以预测seed44应该在94-99%范围内，中值约96.5%。k=0.9 seed44的高SR（>94%预期）与k=0.7 seed44的低SR（~52%预期）共同确认了cliff pattern的seed robustness特性——cliff的具体位置可能存在seed-dependent的浮动，但\"k=0.9 robust, k=0.7 cliff\"的定性模式应该保持不变。\n\n现在用seed43重复OpenVLA的k=0.7随机剪枝实验。基于seed42得到49.0%的结果，我预期seed43会在40-56%的范围内，中值约47%。OpenVLA的性能下降应该是平滑的梯度变化而不像X-VLA那样有cliff point，random pruning虽然增加了额外的随机性，但500个episode的大样本量应该能够稳定这个估计。\n\nMLP投影器的部分独立性意味着不同的随机掩码导致的信息损失相对一致，所以seed42和seed43的结果应该很接近。如果两个seed之间的差异小于5个百分点，就能有信心地说单个seed的结果代表了真实的性能。接下来还要用seed43重复k=0.5的实验，seed42在这个设置下得到37.4%。 Now I'm planning the RoboFlamingo experiment with a Perceiver Resampler connector on LIBERO—this is the fourth connector family to test. I expect it won't finish before the deadline, but if it runs, the baseline should hit around 40-60% success rate with moderate graded degradation under pruning, since the Perceiver uses learnable query tokens to extract fixed-size representations through cross-attention from vision features. Generating taxonomy table...\n\nThe Perceiver Resampler entry would sit around 0.15 CV with moderate graded behavior, though this is planned rather than confirmed. For the paper's scope, the four confirmed connector types across five models and three families already provide solid support for the core taxonomy claims, even if reviewers ask about the missing data—I can argue that our coverage is already the most comprehensive cross-architecture VLA token analysis available.\n\nNow I'm reconsidering what the user meant by \"each planned experiment\"—whether they want predictions for all incomplete entries or just the ones explicitly marked as planned. Looking back at the experiment plan structure, I notice the running X-VLA and OpenVLA seed experiments aren't actually listed in the corresponding experiment IDs, so they might exist outside the formal plan even though they're clearly related work.\n\nI'll include them as additional predictions anyway since they're actively running and connected to the plan entries, then output the final YAML.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2841,"cache_read_input_tokens":57594,"cache_creation"